[{:db/id "q-163576/selection/6e03ecbe0cc56cf8627ed3eb982a5f54d9bde02d09025a256be23be68ab5d8c1" :answer/id #uuid "19e195af-fc39-5744-bea0-e0dfe05792ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163576/selection/0178ce0b76294fbdfdd6243e1d5b03f5664265ee80c1ab55ac1d4c68710d6434" :answer/id #uuid "16494fe4-d0ed-5f9c-bed6-a00ea02f1647" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163576/selection/b1b2260ba03dad007a129b114aa9fbb4dd4be50ab25791e7768231876e1a501b" :answer/id #uuid "049c5f8f-16ae-5f59-9cd8-46a039bd11ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163576/selection/8a135ace4937b1ffa2c52fbce040999428005f5395e9d793e225144a0384a1ba" :answer/id #uuid "bc6eb1e4-6d89-5179-b695-8fc60b311301" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163576/selection/5fd45cec95fc45f99550587cbe4d80dda358c751536fdf37920e2dff6de9568a" :answer/id #uuid "b2308161-7961-54e0-a175-1d02b5e1aa3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163576/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2dd1f937-5a53-5b87-ad77-857d9f4b220d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163576/selection/b1b2260ba03dad007a129b114aa9fbb4dd4be50ab25791e7768231876e1a501b" :answer-field/choices ["q-163576/selection/6e03ecbe0cc56cf8627ed3eb982a5f54d9bde02d09025a256be23be68ab5d8c1" "q-163576/selection/0178ce0b76294fbdfdd6243e1d5b03f5664265ee80c1ab55ac1d4c68710d6434" "q-163576/selection/b1b2260ba03dad007a129b114aa9fbb4dd4be50ab25791e7768231876e1a501b" "q-163576/selection/8a135ace4937b1ffa2c52fbce040999428005f5395e9d793e225144a0384a1ba" "q-163576/selection/5fd45cec95fc45f99550587cbe4d80dda358c751536fdf37920e2dff6de9568a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163576" :question/id #uuid "42754aea-7d8d-54b5-837e-0461d25b662a" :question/math-academy-id "q-163576" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 3=6.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}(8-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{9}[y]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{9}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{y}^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{3}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163576/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bfe2e3e-9d7b-5c53-8de8-2717237d3e9c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163576"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163578/selection/d70de39ed0e663032700fc1a4a360e6c66008c4b3951dbd32c2ad1e395b78aa7" :answer/id #uuid "b20ccb8a-7acc-55e8-bab1-a75ab00e14fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163578/selection/8a27d9e741e21abcd9802bccc25c887e61661711a784c6e9c3a2857f88077b6d" :answer/id #uuid "d27b8a24-f2c9-5eae-aa95-162fdb0c61b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{10}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163578/selection/6f1b1e6d6efb3e49f546f382ebd2796d1934aeda46cab4a4fd746b3290da22d0" :answer/id #uuid "cd1d861d-70b1-5f94-878c-cdf0c652497e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163578/selection/94dfb22f35fa0e8222d9724a1339e2d5ccff11993402bed8870f2f471afbb3cd" :answer/id #uuid "278ade40-aa05-53fd-bb03-5ece8bfbeb8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163578/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" :answer/id #uuid "b89dde50-0f9e-5a7a-a380-c941f631bb7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163578/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "09a3c335-ab68-54bb-a924-2f3f97a04c7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163578/selection/8a27d9e741e21abcd9802bccc25c887e61661711a784c6e9c3a2857f88077b6d" :answer-field/choices ["q-163578/selection/d70de39ed0e663032700fc1a4a360e6c66008c4b3951dbd32c2ad1e395b78aa7" "q-163578/selection/8a27d9e741e21abcd9802bccc25c887e61661711a784c6e9c3a2857f88077b6d" "q-163578/selection/6f1b1e6d6efb3e49f546f382ebd2796d1934aeda46cab4a4fd746b3290da22d0" "q-163578/selection/94dfb22f35fa0e8222d9724a1339e2d5ccff11993402bed8870f2f471afbb3cd" "q-163578/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163578" :question/id #uuid "f102fc37-9019-5b5f-8138-fd88fa02f824" :question/math-academy-id "q-163578" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 3=3.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}(1+9) \\\\  & =\\frac{10M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{0}^{2}=\\frac{10}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{10}{3}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163578/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bfe2e3e-9d7b-5c53-8de8-2717237d3e9c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163578"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-163612"] :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,4\\le y\\le 6}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 2=2.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{6}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{6}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{6}\\frac{1}{3}(1-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{4}^{6}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}[y]_{4}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(6-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-163582/selection/f59323c84f6cabf320cc39357055a0061ffd55f131d77f9b267d146bfe4285c5" :answer/id #uuid "09b0ee51-fd2f-55b3-af7a-877e2a3322b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163582/selection/eceb60566d62f919597959cde53df086bd8acd365efacf7089658306f2b3d833" :answer/id #uuid "7fef4efd-1624-5b4d-aacc-9546dc541e13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163582/selection/a9af996b44e9c3a29868f7b6970e250ded2e7040f92b0ac300531cc11ba4921f" :answer/id #uuid "c9216752-f02e-5757-895c-ba8a27a5f3bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163582/selection/7f76893339431fbe1025dfc34a81e64480edf5168d046d69b36669516297505c" :answer/id #uuid "30c949c4-7a2f-5a4e-89ac-3056df09c554" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163582/selection/3bca3b7c4e38750003df6823f8a15fd4806ae33c173638520b3c8ee8cdb97636" :answer/id #uuid "65672802-b56e-5cdf-b448-d67b8fc900ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163582/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd246c4e-734a-579c-b7b6-4603ef46836e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163582/selection/eceb60566d62f919597959cde53df086bd8acd365efacf7089658306f2b3d833" :answer-field/choices ["q-163582/selection/f59323c84f6cabf320cc39357055a0061ffd55f131d77f9b267d146bfe4285c5" "q-163582/selection/eceb60566d62f919597959cde53df086bd8acd365efacf7089658306f2b3d833" "q-163582/selection/a9af996b44e9c3a29868f7b6970e250ded2e7040f92b0ac300531cc11ba4921f" "q-163582/selection/7f76893339431fbe1025dfc34a81e64480edf5168d046d69b36669516297505c" "q-163582/selection/3bca3b7c4e38750003df6823f8a15fd4806ae33c173638520b3c8ee8cdb97636"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163582" :question/id #uuid "1ac58438-3de5-5bce-96c1-06b2a8754602" :question/math-academy-id "q-163582" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 2=2.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=1}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(\\frac{8}{3}+2{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{7}{3}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{[\\frac{7}{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(7+9-\\frac{7}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{40}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{0}^{2}=\\frac{20}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{20}{3}}=2\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163582/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bfe2e3e-9d7b-5c53-8de8-2717237d3e9c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163582"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-163011"] :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 2=4.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{8}{3}+2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4}{3}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{[\\frac{4}{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(4+9-(\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{1}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(13-\\frac{5}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{34}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{17M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{0}^{2}=\\frac{17}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{3}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-38824"] :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $x={y}^{2}.$ Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=12Mxy.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{x}}{y}^{2}\\cdot 12Mxy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{x}}12x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{1}[3x{y}^{4}]_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{3}-3{x}^{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{[\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{4}-\\frac{3}{10}{x}^{10}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =M(\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{3}{10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9M}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9M}{20}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-38820/selection/9d1439be0b9c29aed8fe15806cf3b93e17cd52920d6627b31f7c8a960562c3a9" :answer/id #uuid "d9c0c337-87a6-5635-9897-82b1a4b66684" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38820/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer/id #uuid "b0f9408f-b5d3-5184-99e4-9a5849d63deb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38820/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "3784ab27-6817-5e75-8e03-9660a1438e9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38820/selection/34a0eb12d8f18c5fad54258b8a975ceb3230c4daa85b9e95bada7c6cd05f669f" :answer/id #uuid "0e85e81b-786d-5ded-91f5-48bb4b426e33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{7}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38820/selection/9fff2a93631149c9cfe9d45dad5ed7a52037d4127b59310adc141f723224290e" :answer/id #uuid "3348d404-dbb8-53ce-9c39-aeaa55ab74cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{7\\sqrt{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38820/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "71d41b46-cece-5da6-8f82-a66347a43318" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-38820/selection/9fff2a93631149c9cfe9d45dad5ed7a52037d4127b59310adc141f723224290e" :answer-field/choices ["q-38820/selection/9d1439be0b9c29aed8fe15806cf3b93e17cd52920d6627b31f7c8a960562c3a9" "q-38820/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" "q-38820/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-38820/selection/34a0eb12d8f18c5fad54258b8a975ceb3230c4daa85b9e95bada7c6cd05f669f" "q-38820/selection/9fff2a93631149c9cfe9d45dad5ed7a52037d4127b59310adc141f723224290e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38820" :question/id #uuid "2d6194c5-1762-5426-8143-928d732b6bf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-38820" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $y={x}^{2},$ the line $x=1,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{20M}{7}(x+y).$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{20M}{7}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{7}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{7}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{x}^{3}y+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y={x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{7}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{5}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{7}{[\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{6}+\\frac{1}{14}{x}^{7}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{7}(\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{14}) \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{7}\\cdot \\frac{5}{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{100M}{147}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{100M}{147}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{100}{147}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{7\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-38820/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38820"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163600/selection/ca7e9f4210b5885b53c4cb152fc69ab7297ba2ff6a6bda56fdba164c4fe81bea" :answer/id #uuid "729cda97-28b4-5e75-b396-d85ea0629325" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163600/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer/id #uuid "63216723-86dd-5ed7-b0c3-effa279969ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163600/selection/a9e249a39e82f48ded5fb654b4049c08b472396d246820b51dfa83b8738ccf06" :answer/id #uuid "d20cdaab-47a4-5b36-8b23-0d8606eb9626" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163600/selection/3ddde6d65b57504d7927970030ff6f47cc633268963c87eff4ee46a732086804" :answer/id #uuid "3eb0cefe-1946-5d9f-8d93-4684d174f423" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163600/selection/e9fe03eb46cc37573ec616cc04dc0d03303ea19a17951a98b1d4a181cc97ecac" :answer/id #uuid "bfe74375-008e-5747-8c6a-9cde25c80c2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163600/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d8f84ea-33ea-5ed0-8e57-33764b41f2fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163600/selection/ca7e9f4210b5885b53c4cb152fc69ab7297ba2ff6a6bda56fdba164c4fe81bea" :answer-field/choices ["q-163600/selection/ca7e9f4210b5885b53c4cb152fc69ab7297ba2ff6a6bda56fdba164c4fe81bea" "q-163600/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" "q-163600/selection/a9e249a39e82f48ded5fb654b4049c08b472396d246820b51dfa83b8738ccf06" "q-163600/selection/3ddde6d65b57504d7927970030ff6f47cc633268963c87eff4ee46a732086804" "q-163600/selection/e9fe03eb46cc37573ec616cc04dc0d03303ea19a17951a98b1d4a181cc97ecac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163600" :question/id #uuid "1b75f6b7-1feb-5cd3-b6ce-f7c0075a6bc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-163600" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the curve $y=\\sqrt{x},$ the line $y=1,$ and the $y$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=12Mxy.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,\\sqrt{x}\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{1}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot 12Mxy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{1}{x}^{3}y+x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}x{y}^{4}]}_{y=\\sqrt{x}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}x)-(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{4}x+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{[\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =12M(\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{1}{16}-\\frac{1}{10}) \\\\  & =12M\\cdot \\frac{7}{80} \\\\  & =\\frac{21M}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{21M}{20}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163600/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163600"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163614/selection/b9eb51e441ee30195dc83b48f69c51745ebf5bc4c29ef9ea23d90fe820a52304" :answer/id #uuid "9a181cf5-af1f-51c2-9ade-207f5eccd245" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163614/selection/8ccbed02bb729da4b256e199c4208413a50bcef8de1b4f5ebffd919a97f68920" :answer/id #uuid "a6781a22-1d4d-5f1e-9a19-8b0f30cdd4fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{22}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163614/selection/3ddde6d65b57504d7927970030ff6f47cc633268963c87eff4ee46a732086804" :answer/id #uuid "c99e2c5c-421a-55ee-ada2-296ef7391ad4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163614/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer/id #uuid "c68a1e04-3a57-5761-9388-b1fc7725f6a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163614/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "60f521be-731f-5cf8-a200-ca375ca4d946" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163614/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "da0954a8-5ca4-5af1-ba8e-132189df6306" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163614/selection/8ccbed02bb729da4b256e199c4208413a50bcef8de1b4f5ebffd919a97f68920" :answer-field/choices ["q-163614/selection/b9eb51e441ee30195dc83b48f69c51745ebf5bc4c29ef9ea23d90fe820a52304" "q-163614/selection/8ccbed02bb729da4b256e199c4208413a50bcef8de1b4f5ebffd919a97f68920" "q-163614/selection/3ddde6d65b57504d7927970030ff6f47cc633268963c87eff4ee46a732086804" "q-163614/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" "q-163614/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163614" :question/id #uuid "afafc33f-cb3e-5594-b630-d8df16a9a255" :question/math-academy-id "q-163614" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the curves $y={x}^{3}$ and $y={x}^{2}.$ Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=20Mx.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le {x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{{x}^{2}}{y}^{2}\\cdot 20Mx\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =20M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{{x}^{2}}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =20M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{3}x{y}^{3}]}_{y={x}^{3}}^{y={x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{7}-{x}^{10}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{3}{[\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{8}-\\frac{1}{11}{x}^{11}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{3}(\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{1}{11}) \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{88} \\\\  & =\\frac{5M}{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{5M}{22}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{22}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163614/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163614"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-163604"] :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the lines $y=x,$ $x=2,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3}{4}My.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le x}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}My\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{[\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}\\cdot \\frac{16}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{12M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{12M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{12}{5}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-163657/selection/0ff0c61a3c874ed473794d395548e842d78ce9478395a0ce2d41ffd7b4ec450e" :answer/id #uuid "a08c0d15-519b-5833-bf89-f478d5d65d89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163657/selection/99522c389bf97ae913910ff3f72f66dcbe53251c0f44b1e38c6583e21df32da9" :answer/id #uuid "92674799-0b41-5422-bd97-ecc681558abe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163657/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "f00fffb7-fa7b-5270-b6a6-58859f3f4cfa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163657/selection/324ac0c1790f4041f137fa50b4b839fba20ebf09af4d8ea28cd44ee96ed6f4bb" :answer/id #uuid "f81728d3-164e-5677-af8f-f16be9f2feda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163657/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "6165bbc0-de39-5bec-a731-cc429253e058" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163657/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c705de2f-b369-5420-971d-96cd88370316" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163657/selection/99522c389bf97ae913910ff3f72f66dcbe53251c0f44b1e38c6583e21df32da9" :answer-field/choices ["q-163657/selection/0ff0c61a3c874ed473794d395548e842d78ce9478395a0ce2d41ffd7b4ec450e" "q-163657/selection/99522c389bf97ae913910ff3f72f66dcbe53251c0f44b1e38c6583e21df32da9" "q-163657/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" "q-163657/selection/324ac0c1790f4041f137fa50b4b839fba20ebf09af4d8ea28cd44ee96ed6f4bb" "q-163657/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163657" :question/id #uuid "a99d2798-c187-5104-9954-2eb7a502ad0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-163657" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region between two circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }{x}^{2}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{5}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{1}^{2}({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{21}{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{\\theta }{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }{4}]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{5\\pi }\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{14M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-163657/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "068d9714-bd1e-5036-a0c7-9be288831f52"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163657"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163650/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "ef045a0f-cfe3-5ab9-aa0e-cdbd03c3cacf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163650/selection/a272cbe64fea514fe5c8c9685aef2c9378fdfe44c54941c8bcba64a5f713bc84" :answer/id #uuid "99b42a1f-ecf9-5bfd-b64d-391a6c4b210b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163650/selection/84aaba064027e7eb0bf329f6bc084c93277c0b932bcb0178f06baf24c9b9c48a" :answer/id #uuid "a0e5cc8b-2506-50d2-afa5-32fc1168679d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163650/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "d1782786-c99e-5706-95f4-e348e16fd5b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163650/selection/a2bf9f278822239fe980121e1c2efe6b2a1075aef929e587d78abba90e1e8b5d" :answer/id #uuid "3d6ac81d-a1a8-5904-9aaa-112cd57680b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163650/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a73b21b-8693-53c9-b09c-068d274ba5bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163650/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-163650/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-163650/selection/a272cbe64fea514fe5c8c9685aef2c9378fdfe44c54941c8bcba64a5f713bc84" "q-163650/selection/84aaba064027e7eb0bf329f6bc084c93277c0b932bcb0178f06baf24c9b9c48a" "q-163650/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-163650/selection/a2bf9f278822239fe980121e1c2efe6b2a1075aef929e587d78abba90e1e8b5d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163650" :question/id #uuid "9acf39a4-64d3-553b-9958-8b97a070f182" :question/math-academy-id "q-163650" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the part of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 2$ for $x\\ge 0.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{2M}{\\pi }{y}^{2}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{2M}{\\pi }{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{5}{sin}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{\\pi }({\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{4}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot ({\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{(\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}\\cdot ({\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡2\\theta }{4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{8M}{3\\pi }\\cdot ({\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡2\\theta }{4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{8M}{3\\pi }\\cdot ({\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +1}{8}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{8M}{3\\pi }\\cdot ({\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{3}{8}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta }{8}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{8M}{3\\pi }\\cdot {[\\frac{3\\theta }{8}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }{4}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }{32}]}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8M}{3\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{8} \\\\  & =M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{M\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-163650/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "068d9714-bd1e-5036-a0c7-9be288831f52"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163650"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163645/selection/cd27863173b47e1c5fbea48fb97141526856e3af9aaba24db91ecebcf356bae8" :answer/id #uuid "edf2cee5-b9f7-5ce9-9087-ff275f94b555" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{15}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163645/selection/c5de85b82cd96130e763764b15d80e2f9efdc5b512670420c290d671194d845d" :answer/id #uuid "61a26b23-b857-5874-9afe-162898090845" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{93}{70}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163645/selection/5abad7e7c12267f00cfd275a548cf625762f39cb79d9d3298b8d4c13ae172bf4" :answer/id #uuid "8ef513dd-a601-5bcc-abf7-45c89edbb091" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{67}{60}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163645/selection/0178ce0b76294fbdfdd6243e1d5b03f5664265ee80c1ab55ac1d4c68710d6434" :answer/id #uuid "62463465-16ae-52e2-b1ad-3819c738909f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163645/selection/bcb141c4ae681d189bde07fd393db705f6344e5a0328485d0d7cfa5adbbfe888" :answer/id #uuid "f5eb56e5-70bf-5f9a-b83c-37be34b75d59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{52}{41}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163645/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4399627a-a895-52a7-a0ea-7efa0df9ce90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163645/selection/c5de85b82cd96130e763764b15d80e2f9efdc5b512670420c290d671194d845d" :answer-field/choices ["q-163645/selection/cd27863173b47e1c5fbea48fb97141526856e3af9aaba24db91ecebcf356bae8" "q-163645/selection/c5de85b82cd96130e763764b15d80e2f9efdc5b512670420c290d671194d845d" "q-163645/selection/5abad7e7c12267f00cfd275a548cf625762f39cb79d9d3298b8d4c13ae172bf4" "q-163645/selection/0178ce0b76294fbdfdd6243e1d5b03f5664265ee80c1ab55ac1d4c68710d6434" "q-163645/selection/bcb141c4ae681d189bde07fd393db705f6344e5a0328485d0d7cfa5adbbfe888"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163645" :question/id #uuid "5a55592d-e97d-5673-88f1-e39a7437cfff" :question/math-academy-id "q-163645" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies region bounded by two circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3}{14\\pi }M\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{3}{14\\pi }Mr.$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{14\\pi }M{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{r}^{5}{|}_{1}^{2}\\cdot ({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )}{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{31}{5}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}\\theta -\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{31}{5}\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{93M}{70}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{93M}{70}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{93}{70}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-163645/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "068d9714-bd1e-5036-a0c7-9be288831f52"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163645"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-38825"] :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the part of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4$ in the first quadrant. Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3}{8}Mx.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{3}{8}Mr\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}M{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{4}{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}M({\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}M\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{r}^{5}{|}_{0}^{2}\\cdot ({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{12M}{5}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta }{3}]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12M}{5}(1-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{8M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{8}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-163594/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "6fea5c47-7dca-52ef-80db-584acd1cd454" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163594/selection/94dfb22f35fa0e8222d9724a1339e2d5ccff11993402bed8870f2f471afbb3cd" :answer/id #uuid "53086998-2c28-53ca-9caa-cf03493be237" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163594/selection/b1b2260ba03dad007a129b114aa9fbb4dd4be50ab25791e7768231876e1a501b" :answer/id #uuid "552ec8db-ab66-5495-912a-a61bbcf5c11b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163594/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "4dc8c3d1-413d-544b-9266-8cc15bf82ccc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163594/selection/c24232afb9b5ba9c1cc5619273d09a5676ecc0aa44d228853ae38c1edcbf08e1" :answer/id #uuid "629729fa-bbe3-5f4a-960b-a75563f95ecb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163594/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "85e903b2-e31d-50b2-afca-dfb20dadf9b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163594/selection/c24232afb9b5ba9c1cc5619273d09a5676ecc0aa44d228853ae38c1edcbf08e1" :answer-field/choices ["q-163594/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-163594/selection/94dfb22f35fa0e8222d9724a1339e2d5ccff11993402bed8870f2f471afbb3cd" "q-163594/selection/b1b2260ba03dad007a129b114aa9fbb4dd4be50ab25791e7768231876e1a501b" "q-163594/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-163594/selection/c24232afb9b5ba9c1cc5619273d09a5676ecc0aa44d228853ae38c1edcbf08e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163594" :question/id #uuid "41711bc6-3248-5171-a778-081733948b48" :question/math-academy-id "q-163594" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 3.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{4}{9\\pi }M{x}^{2}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{4}{9\\pi }M{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9\\pi }M{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{r}^{5}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{9\\pi }({\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot ({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}\\cdot ({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2\\pi }\\cdot ({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta )}{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2\\pi }\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}\\theta -\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta ]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2\\pi }\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-163594/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "068d9714-bd1e-5036-a0c7-9be288831f52"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163594"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12487"] :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 3, \\:\\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 2 \\big\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda(x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_x$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n$R_x = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_x}{M}},$\nwhere $I_x$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_y$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n$R_y = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_y}{M}},$\nwhere $I_y$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_0$ about the origin is given by\n$R_0 = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_0}{M}},$\nwhere $I_0$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\nI_y = \\iint\\limits_D x^2\\lambda(x,y) \\:\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $\\mathcal{A} =  3\\cdot 1 = 3.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = \\dfrac{M}{\\mathcal{A}} = \\dfrac{M}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}9\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3M[y]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =3M(2-1) \\\\  & =3M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nR_y^2 =\\dfrac{3M}{M} =  3\\quad \\Rightarrow\\quad R_y = \\sqrt{3}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12507"] :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the lines $y = x,$ $x = 1,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda(x,y) = 3Mx.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda(x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_x$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n$R_x = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_x}{M}},$\nwhere $I_x$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_y$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n$R_y = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_y}{M}},$\nwhere $I_y$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_0$ about the origin is given by\n$R_0 = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_0}{M}},$\nwhere $I_0$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\nI_0 = \\iint\\limits_D (x^2 + y^2) \\lambda(x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{(x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq x \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot 3Mx\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{x}^{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}x{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{[\\frac{4}{15}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =3M\\cdot \\frac{4}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12495"] :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies one-half of the circle $x^2+y^2\\leq 1$ for $y\\geq 0.$ Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda(x,y)=\\dfrac{3}{2}My.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda(x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_x$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n$R_x = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_x}{M}},$\nwhere $I_x$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_y$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n$R_y = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_y}{M}},$\nwhere $I_y$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_0$ about the origin is given by\n$R_0 = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_0}{M}},$\nwhere $I_0$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (r,\\theta) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq r \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\pi \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\nI_0 = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda(r,\\theta) r^3 \\:\\textrm{d}r\\:\\textrm{d}\\theta,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(r,\\theta)$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda(r,\\theta)=\\dfrac{3}{2}Mr\\sin\\theta.$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}M{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}{r}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}M({\\int }_{0}^{1}{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}M\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{r}^{5}{|}_{0}^{1}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}M\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
